time is almost up for boris johnson's  premiership but is he leaving behind a  dark secret at the heart of his  government  a sky news investigation spanning months  looking into westminster culture can  reveal allegations of sexual misconduct  that go right to the top against a  serving cabinet minister and a senior  number 10 aide  to protect the alleged victims we've  allowed them to speak anonymously so  these aren't them you will see all their  voices but these are their stories in  their words i was sexually assaulted by  someone who's now a cabinet minister i  was in my early twenties and  didn't really know how to deal with it i  was super drunk he's feeding me more  wine and i'm already quite obviously  tanked but after a while i was like you  know what would you mind if i just went  to bed so i went to bed but obviously he  didn't leave me alone i woke up the next  morning and i realized what had happened  i reported it to an mp i worked for a  couple of years later  and i did go to the police years later  as well  and had a very brief chat with them  and decided not to proceed with a formal  complaint  because they couldn't give me any  reassurances until i made a formal  statement  i was too scared to kick start that  process and risk it spiraling out of  control  the second allegation concerns number  ten at the time the alleged victim had a  senior role in downing street the man  she accuses was attached to a political  campaign  i was working a conservative event at an  evening reception i was with a number of  colleagues in this room it was pretty  like crowded sweaty  full of men and basically i felt someone  grab my ass and i turned around and this  guy was just like looking right at me  she complained and then when she heard  he was about to get a top job in number  10 she raised it again  nothing happened i think my mind was  really opened basically about how far  people will go to protect people and  keep things quiet and basically just  brush everything under the carpet  when his boss a close aide to boris  johnson was made aware of the allegation  she claims he dismissed it others have  confirmed this i was told that the guy  who hired him said oh he's a  good-looking man he wouldn't do that he  has women throwing themselves at him he  said that to a few people  in relation to the first allegation a  government spokesperson said we take  allegations of misconduct extremely  seriously and there are robust  procedures in place to raise concerns  all ministerial appointments also follow  established processes  in relation to the second allegation a  government spokesperson said all  prospective government employees are  subject to necessary checks and vetting  we do not comment on individuals  a conservative spokesperson said there  is an established code of conduct and  complaints procedure where people can  report complaints in confidence we take  any complaint seriously  these allegations emerged during a  long-running sky news investigation we  spoke to people who work in westminster  at all levels from all political parties  and heard numerous accounts of sexual  misconduct and bullying there was a fear  among some that speaking out could end  their career others told us that these  stories circulate as gossip and rumor  but often no action is taken  what we found was that despite many  attempts over the years to change it  there is still a toxic culture here that  goes to the very highest levels of  british politics  are you doing anything to deal with your  party's toxic culture prime minister  boris johnson's premiership was marred  by a series of sexual misconduct  scandals including the one that  eventually brought him down the  resignation of his deputy chief whip  chris pincher amid allegations of  groping two men at a conservative  private members club mr pinscher what  exactly happened in the carton club  but it wasn't just the allegations it  was the question of who knew what and  when  and now that more have surfaced what  does this say about the prime minister's  time in office do you have any um  regrets at all over how you've dealt  with the um sexual allegations of  misconduct look i think all those  they're very they have all those things  have to be handled uh carefully and  sensibly and we have uh processes  for dealing with them  a shadow hangs over westminster but  change is coming it will be for the next  prime minister to say how they will get  culture here under control for good liz  bates sky news
 

